100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 297 0 R
/E (Positivity Bias: The combined rating of 4 stars and 5 stars accounts for 57% of all ratings made. Users are rating movies they have typically already identified as something they will likely enjoy. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 298 0 R
/E (Long-Tail Users: The majority of users rate very few movies; therefore a small proportion of users \(the "super users"\) account for the largest proportion of all ratings. This creates a "cold-start" problem for the majority of movies.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 299 0 R
/E (Popularity Skew: A small number of movies receive 1,000's of ratings while most receive very few; therefore, the models must be designed to minimize recommending already-popular movies.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
